        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "wheel-test-bench"
        },
        "markdown": "## Setup\n\n1. Open this graph in edit or view mode, zoomed so a fixture fills a good part of the screen.\n2. To check by hand, put the pointer over a fixture and use the wheel. Try Ctrl or Cmd with the wheel and a trackpad pinch too.\n3. To check every case at once, paste the **Check Script** into the browser console and run `await runWheelBench()`.\n4. For the workspace-level case, open **Wheel Test Page** with its portal, then zoom out until it is drawn as part of the workspace.\n\nThe bench does not change any graph data."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "wheel-test-bench-cases",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Cases",
      "position": {
        "x": -700,
        "y": 400
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 640,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "wheel-test-bench"
        },
        "markdown": "## Cases (the contract)\n\n| # | Pointer is over | Gesture | Expected under the contract |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Long document, mid-scroll | wheel down | The **surface** keeps the wheel and scrolls. The camera does not move or zoom. |\n| 2 | Tall HTML page | wheel down | The page scrolls. Camera does not move or zoom. |\n| 3 | Nested scroller, inner box not at its end | wheel down | The **inner** box scrolls first; the outer page does not. |\n| 4 | Nested scroller, inner box at its end | wheel down | The outer page scrolls (scroll chaining). |\n| 5 | Long document, at its end | wheel down | The camera **pans**. |\n| 6 | Nothing to scroll | wheel down | The camera **pans**. |\n| 7 | Empty canvas | wheel down | The camera **pans**. |\n| 8 | Empty canvas | Ctrl + wheel | The camera **zooms**, and the point under the pointer stays put. Page zoom is prevented. |\n| 9 | Wheel Test Page, drawn at workspace level | wheel down | The page scrolls, then chains to the camera at its end. |\n\nCase 9 is checked by hand: it needs the second graph opened next to this one.\n\nThe gestures that a browser handles itself (menu zoom, and the keyboard zoom keys in some browsers) cannot be triggered by a script. Check those by hand and record the result in Observations."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "wheel-test-bench-check-script",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Check Script",
      "position": {
        "x": 460,
        "y": 400
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 700,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "wheel-test-bench"
        },
        "markdown": "## Check Script\n\nPaste this into the browser console with the bench open, then run `await runWheelBench()`. It moves the camera between cases, sends wheel events over each fixture, and prints one row per case: who took the wheel, who the contract says should take it, and whether they match. \"surface\" means the surface under the pointer kept the wheel (it scrolled, or the event was left alone for the browser to scroll); \"pan\" and \"zoom\" mean the camera took it. Script-made events cannot scroll anything natively, so this measures who claims the wheel, and a real wheel or trackpad is still needed to see the scrolling itself. It changes no graph data.\n\n```js\nasync function runWheelBench() {\n  const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, ms));\n  const api = window.graphAPI;\n  const canvas = document.getElementById('graph-canvas') || document.body;\n  const box = () => canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const camera = () => { const v = api.getViewport(); return { x: v.pan.x, y: v.pan.y, zoom: v.zoom }; };\n  const inNode = (el) => Boolean(el && el.closest('[data-node-id],[data-node-draggable],[data-node-interactive],[data-workspace-instance]'));\n  // A node's element sits at its graph position, scaled and panned by the camera.\n  const nodeEl = (id) => {\n    const n = api.readNode(id).data;\n    const c = camera();\n    return [...document.querySelectorAll('.node-or-handle')].find((el) =>\n      Math.abs(parseFloat(el.style.left) - (n.position.x * c.zoom + c.x)) < 2 && Math.abs(parseFloat(el.style.top) - (n.position.y * c.zoom + c.y)) < 2) || null;\n  };\n\n  // Put a node in the middle of the screen at zoom 1.\n  const center = async (id) => {\n    const n = api.readNode(id).data;\n    const r = box();\n    api.setViewport({ zoom: 1, pan: { x: r.width / 2 - (n.position.x + n.width / 2), y: r.height / 2 - (n.position.y + n.height / 2) } });\n    await sleep(700);\n  };\n  // The scroll regions inside a node, outermost first.\n  const regions = (el) => [el, ...el.querySelectorAll('*')].filter((e) => /^(auto|scroll)$/.test(getComputedStyle(e).overflowY) && e.scrollHeight > e.clientHeight + 2);\n  const send = (target, x, y, deltaY, ctrlKey = false) => {\n    const event = new WheelEvent('wheel', { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, clientX: x, clientY: y, deltaY, deltaMode: 0, ctrlKey });\n    target.dispatchEvent(event);\n    return event.defaultPrevented;\n  };\n\n  // One case: what moved when the wheel was used at (x, y)?\n  const attempt = async ({ x, y, deltaY, ctrlKey, watch }) => {\n    const before = { camera: camera(), scroll: watch.map((e) => e.scrollTop) };\n    const target = document.elementFromPoint(x, y) || canvas;\n    const prevented = send(target, x, y, deltaY, ctrlKey);\n    await sleep(500);\n    const after = { camera: camera(), scroll: watch.map((e) => e.scrollTop) };\n    const rect = box();\n    const graphAt = (c) => ({ x: (x - rect.left - c.x) / c.zoom, y: (y - rect.top - c.y) / c.zoom });\n    return {\n      prevented,\n      scrolled: watch.map((e, i) => Math.round(after.scroll[i] - before.scroll[i])),\n      zoomed: Math.abs(after.camera.zoom - before.camera.zoom) > 0.001,\n      panned: Math.hypot(after.camera.x - before.camera.x, after.camera.y - before.camera.y) > 0.5 && Math.abs(after.camera.zoom - before.camera.zoom) <= 0.001,\n      pointerHeld: Math.hypot(graphAt(after.camera).x - graphAt(before.camera).x, graphAt(after.camera).y - graphAt(before.camera).y) < 1.5\n    };\n  };\n  // Script-made wheel events cannot scroll anything natively, so the script measures who claimed the wheel:\n  // 'surface' means the surface under the pointer kept it (it scrolled, or the event was left alone for the\n  // browser to scroll); 'zoom' and 'pan' mean the camera took it.\n  const did = (r) => (r.zoomed ? 'zoom' : r.panned ? 'pan' : (r.scrolled.some((s) => s !== 0) || !r.prevented) ? 'surface' : 'nothing');\n  const rows = [];\n  const record = (id, name, expected, result, extra = {}) => rows.push({ case: id, over: name, expected, did: did(result), ok: did(result) === expected && (extra.check ? extra.check(result) : true), ...result });\n  const measure = (id) => nodeEl(id)?.getBoundingClientRect();\n\n  // 1. Long document, mid-scroll\n  await center('wheel-test-bench-long-doc');\n  let el = nodeEl('wheel-test-bench-long-doc'); let r = measure('wheel-test-bench-long-doc');\n  let watch = regions(el);\n  record(1, 'Long document, mid-scroll', 'surface', await attempt({ x: r.left + r.width / 2, y: r.top + r.height / 2, deltaY: 120, watch }));\n\n  // 2. Tall HTML page\n  await center('wheel-test-bench-tall-html');\n  el = nodeEl('wheel-test-bench-tall-html'); r = measure('wheel-test-bench-tall-html'); watch = regions(el);\n  record(2, 'Tall HTML page', 'surface', await attempt({ x: r.left + r.width / 2, y: r.top + r.height / 2, deltaY: 120, watch }));\n\n  // 3 and 4. Nested scroller\n  await center('wheel-test-bench-nested');\n  el = nodeEl('wheel-test-bench-nested'); r = measure('wheel-test-bench-nested'); watch = regions(el);\n  const inner = watch.find((e) => e.id === 'inner') || watch[watch.length - 1];\n  const outer = watch.find((e) => e !== inner);\n  inner.scrollTop = 0;\n  const box3 = inner.getBoundingClientRect();\n  record(3, 'Nested scroller, inner box not at its end', 'surface', await attempt({ x: box3.left + box3.width / 2, y: box3.top + box3.height / 2, deltaY: 60, watch: [inner, outer].filter(Boolean) }), {\n    check: (res) => !res.prevented\n  });\n  inner.scrollTop = inner.scrollHeight;\n  await sleep(200);\n  record(4, 'Nested scroller, inner box at its end', 'surface', await attempt({ x: box3.left + box3.width / 2, y: box3.top + box3.height / 2, deltaY: 60, watch: [inner, outer].filter(Boolean) }), {\n    check: (res) => !res.prevented\n  });\n\n  // 5. Long document, at its end\n  await center('wheel-test-bench-long-doc');\n  el = nodeEl('wheel-test-bench-long-doc'); r = measure('wheel-test-bench-long-doc'); watch = regions(el);\n  watch.forEach((e) => { e.scrollTop = e.scrollHeight; });\n  await sleep(200);\n  record(5, 'Long document, at its end', 'pan', await attempt({ x: r.left + r.width / 2, y: r.top + r.height / 2, deltaY: 120, watch }));\n\n  // 6. Nothing to scroll\n  await center('wheel-test-bench-short');\n  el = nodeEl('wheel-test-bench-short'); r = measure('wheel-test-bench-short');\n  record(6, 'Nothing to scroll', 'pan', await attempt({ x: r.left + r.width / 2, y: r.top + r.height / 2, deltaY: 120, watch: regions(el) }));\n\n  // 7 and 8. Empty canvas: a point below the label, with no node under it\n  await center('wheel-test-bench-empty-label');\n  const label = measure('wheel-test-bench-empty-label');\n  const empty = { x: label.left + label.width / 2, y: label.bottom + 180 };\n  const under = document.elementFromPoint(empty.x, empty.y);\n  if (inNode(under)) {\n    rows.push({ case: '7-8', over: 'Empty canvas', expected: 'pan / zoom', did: 'blocked', ok: false, note: `a node is under the pointer: ${under && under.tagName}` });\n  } else {\n    record(7, 'Empty canvas', 'pan', await attempt({ x: empty.x, y: empty.y, deltaY: 120, watch: [] }));\n    await center('wheel-test-bench-empty-label');\n    record(8, 'Empty canvas, Ctrl + wheel', 'zoom', await attempt({ x: empty.x, y: empty.y, deltaY: -120, ctrlKey: true, watch: [] }), {\n      check: (res) => res.prevented && res.pointerHeld\n    });\n  }\n\n  const table = rows.map((row) => ({\n    case: row.case, over: row.over, expected: row.expected, did: row.did, matches: row.ok ? 'yes' : 'NO',\n    prevented: row.prevented, scrolled: JSON.stringify(row.scrolled), zoomed: row.zoomed, panned: row.panned, pointerHeld: row.pointerHeld\n  }));\n  console.table(table);\n  console.log(`${rows.filter((row) => row.ok).length} of ${rows.length} cases match the contract`);\n  return table;\n}\n\n```"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "wheel-test-bench-observations",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Observations",
      "position": {
        "x": -120,
        "y": 400
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 620,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "wheel-test-bench"
        },
        "markdown": "## Observations\n\n### Run 1: script, headless Edge, dev build of the working tree\n\n4 of 8 cases match the contract. Script-made events cannot scroll natively, so this measures who took the wheel.\n\n| # | Over | Expected | Did | Match |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Long document, mid-scroll | surface | surface | yes |\n| 2 | Tall HTML page | surface | surface | yes |\n| 3 | Nested scroller, inner not at end | surface | surface | yes |\n| 4 | Nested scroller, inner at end | surface | surface | yes |\n| 5 | Long document, at its end | pan | surface | **no** |\n| 6 | Nothing to scroll | pan | surface | **no** |\n| 7 | Empty canvas | pan | zoom | **no** |\n| 8 | Empty canvas, Ctrl + wheel | zoom under the pointer | zoom about the screen centre | **no** |\n\n### What the run shows\n\n- **Over a content node the canvas never gets the wheel.** Cases 5 and 6: at the end of a document, or over a card with nothing to scroll, the event is not cancelled and nothing moves, so the camera cannot be moved with the wheel from there. The node listener stops the event before the canvas handler sees it.\n- **On empty canvas the wheel zooms (7), and does it about the middle of the screen, not the pointer.** The point under the pointer moved by hundreds of pixels.\n- **Ctrl + wheel is treated as a plain wheel (8).** It zooms, but about the screen centre, and the point under the pointer does not stay put.\n- Not yet checked: case 9 (a graph at workspace level), by hand, and menu zoom."
      }
    },
